  "solution": {
    "text": "<table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 100%;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Colour</td>\t\t\t<td>Letter as an aid to memory</td>\t\t\t<td>Number</td>\t\t\t<td>Multiplier</td>\t\t\t<td>Colour</td>\t\t\t<td>Tolerance</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Black</td>\t\t\t<td>B</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>0</mn></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Gold</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>%</mo></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Brown</td>\t\t\t<td>B</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>1</mn></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>Silver</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Red</td>\t\t\t<td>R</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>\t\t\t<p>No fourth band</p>\t\t\t</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Orange</td>\t\t\t<td>O</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Yellow</td>\t\t\t<td>Y</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Green</td>\t\t\t<td>G</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>5</mn></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Blue</td>\t\t\t<td>B</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Violet</td>\t\t\t<td>V</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>7</mn></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>Grey</td>\t\t\t<td>G</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>8</mn></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>White</td>\t\t\t<td>W</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math></td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup></math></td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td>&nbsp;</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table><p>A set of coloured co-axial rings or bands is printed on the resistor which reveals the following facts :<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The first band indicates the first significant figure.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The second band indicates the second significant figure.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The third band indicates the power of ten with which the above two significant figures must be multiplied to get the resistance value in ohms.<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The fourth band indicates the tolerance or possible variation in percent of the indicated value. If the fourth band is absent, it implies a tolerance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/42d53fd8-d6bc-4a00-be93-be5c1fd000d8-image.png\" style=\"width: 456px; height: 228px;\" /></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>7500</mn><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>375</mn><mo>)</mo><mi>&#937;</mi></math></p>",
